msgctxt "/AB3C920D496177C6E72CC0B4F8BA9F53"
msgid ""
"00:00\n"
"At onset, I’m skeptical of the subject’s aptitude for conditioning. He "
"appears to ramble to himself and seems to struggle with focusing. His eyes "
"dart around, as if looking for something. Can’t say what at this point. Those "
"assigned to ask questions ensured us that he was ready. However, given our "
"recent track record, I’m skeptical.\n"
"\n"
"01:24\n"
"The subject has begun shouting a name, but he struggles to enunciate "
"properly. Louis? Lucy? Likely, the meshing of bone, muscle, and plush with "
"the medium is the culprit here. Will continue to monitor and "
"note.\n"
"\n"
"08:46\n"
"Seven more hours in, and the subject appears to have quieted. Less thrashing "
"against the restraints. Less muttering. \n"
"\n"
"12:32\n"
"While making my rounds, the subject appeared to be singing and tapping his "
"foot against his restraints.\n"
"\n"
"12:36\n"
"Subject is now repeating:\n"
"\n"
"“Joy. I live it. I feel it. I am it.”\n"
"\n"
"14:00\n"
"After additional observation time, I can confidently say that the subject’s "
"conditioning is now complete. Approved. F"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "/A8C1D1ED48062EFDA90B10BE5C0EDBB7"
msgid ""
"08/06/1995\n"
"Project Proposal\n"
"Experiment # 1468\n"
"Tags: Bigger Bodies Initiative\n"
"\n"
"Abstract\n"
"In accordance with prior conversation and critical feedback, proposed "
"operational procedures and materials for Experiment 1468 have seen a radical "
"shift. Rather than each strand of “hair” being comprised of a sequence of "
"grafted finger bones and muscle in a loose hair facade, we’ve allocated horse "
"hair (for its tensile strength, durability, and flexibility), an artificial "
"bone construction, and various biological materials, which we’ve listed "
"below.\n"
"\n"
" Neural integration protocols have shown promising responsiveness in trials, "
"indicating the subject’s cognitive link will extend naturally to the hair "
"construct. In effect, Lily’s mind will be able to manipulate each and every "
"strand as if it were its own limb. As such, our crafting will need to be "
"intricate and operated by our most delicate hands.\n"
"\n"
"Materials and Methods\n"
"Ahead of August 20th’s operation, extracted capillaries will be required for "
"the attenuation of pain responses and\n"
"(Note cuts off)"
msgstr ""

