msgctxt "/27EA0B93421F091830ABAAB9C15F7737"
msgid ""
"Leith has asked us to remove any Wrongside Outimals branding from our "
"workspace (murals, cutouts, etc). Apparently, they focus-tested very poorly, "
"and it’s been decided they won’t be going into production; the whole toy line "
"is getting scrapped.\n"
"\n"
"I wouldn’t rush to do it, though. Remember, Leith made the same request about "
"Daisy, and she’s still plastered all over the place.\n"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "/D893D87C4CDBFF40BFC27781EDCC1DF9"
msgid ""
"Leith,\n"
"Given the… sensitive… nature of this subject, I suggest we make use of the "
"neural mapper. We can run the process in parallel with normal procedure, "
"having one of the resulting versions put to work, and the other stored "
"somewhere for safe keeping. Hell, shove it in with the computer servers and "
"call it a day, no need to be fancy about it.\n"
"\n"
"-Dr. White\n"
"\n"
"Do it. -LP"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "/F70B33F14D862FDB55E75AB3A7394A35"
msgid ""
"Leith,\n"
"I’m pleased to say that one of my pet projects has had a breakthrough. During "
"our latest attempt at neural mapping, we were able to successfully record and "
"reconstruct brief subjective moments from our subject’s short-term "
"memory.\n"
"\n"
"If we can scale this practice, it could give a whole new dimension to our "
"work. \n"
"\n"
"Think about it; how many subjects can we realistically pull from Home Sweet "
"Home? 30% 50%? I can hardly imagine this being sustainable in the long-term. "
"If, however, we use the mapper, it could allow us to completely reconstruct a "
"subject’s psyche based on prior imaging. We could do this as many times as "
"needed, provided we have the proteins and lipids. That is to say, "
"duplication. Were that the case, we’d never need to worry about a shortage of "
"test candidates again.\n"
"\n"
"-Dr. Sawyer"
msgstr ""

