msgctxt "/9F1F47A744BEF5EE62E74AAFD402BC96"
msgid ""
"Managerial Note: All first-time employees, please follow these procedures "
"absolutely to the letter. Our work is both sensitive and vital to the success "
"of the operation. Please, follow these instructions to the letter.\n"
"\n"
"STEP #1: Ensure cleanliness from decontamination (Specimens mustn’t be "
"infected with outside contaminants.)\n"
"\n"
"STEP #2: Wear ALL required hazmat hardware. \n"
"\n"
"STEP #3: Acquire specimens \n"
"\n"
"STEP #4: Clean specimens (Ensure blood, stains, debris, teeth, etc., are all "
"removed from the specimen.)\n"
"\n"
"STEP #5: Using proper tools, carefully remove the specimen’s skin, being "
"cautious not to damage valuable tissue beneath. (When necessary, use the de-"
"threader.)\n"
"\n"
"STEP #6: Distill the specimen (Warning: This is the messiest stage of the "
"process.)\n"
"\n"
"STEP #7: Collect extracted Poppy Gel in specialized containers. (If we’re out "
"of containers, please let me know.)\n"
"\n"
"STEP #8: Dispose of the remnants in the Boilers.\n"
"\n"
"(Hand-written) My Advice– Use the term “specimens” when referring to your "
"work. Believe me, you’ll sleep a lot easier if you do.\n"
"\n"
"Sincerely,\n"
"North Geisler \n"
"Lead Mortician"
msgstr ""

