msgctxt "/12124C3A43CE8E85263A4B94BD600EDD"
msgid ""
"Where to even begin with this nightmare of a week? They were hiding down in "
"Playcare, probably for several weeks, and somehow nobody noticed. If it "
"weren’t for the accident with that Theodore child, I’m not sure we’d have "
"discovered them at all (or Elliot’s body). At any rate, Theodore’s “imaginary "
"friend” won’t talk to anyone, but the girl- the one Elliot’s notes called "
"“1007”- is a bit more cooperative.\n"
"\n"
"I feel like a moron just writing this part. She introduced herself as Poppy. "
"Not just the doll but the girl the dolls were made after: Poppy Ludwig. She "
"remembered me, how we met. She had the same voice and everything. It was made "
"only more unnerving by the fact that she seemed downright traumatized by the "
"whole ordeal.\n"
"\n"
"It’s impossible, isn’t it? That girl’s been gone a long time.\n"
"\n"
"There’s more though. Things my investigator dug up from an office Elliot had "
"tucked away. Most of it is trashed, but there are pieces. I still don’t know "
"what to make of it. All I know for sure is something big has been going on "
"under our noses, and whatever it is, I think it might have gotten the old man "
"killed."
msgstr ""

